      "final_text": "美国宏观：上周美国宏观经济日历较为繁忙。通胀数据低于预期，6月核心消费者价格指数环比持平，而市场共识预期为 +0.2%；核心生产者价格指数环比 +0.2%，而市场共识预期为 +0.4%。6月零售销售超出预期，反映出消费者支出具有韧性。密歇根大学消费者信心指数初值为54.4，高于市场共识预期51.0；1年期通胀预期下降0.4个百分点至4.2%。加息预期波动较大，最终稳定在年底前累计加息约30个基点，较上周下降6个基点，但仍低于周初因中东局势升温所推动的逾40个基点的高点。",
      "iterations": 0,
      "seg_status": "machine",
      "source_text": "U.S. macro: Last week’s U.S. macro calendar was busy. Inflation was softer than expected with June core CPI flat m/m vs consensus +0.2%, while core PPI was +0.2% m/m vs consensus +0.4%. June retail sales beat expectations, reflecting resilient consumer spending. Preliminary UMich Consumer Sentiment beat at 54.4 vs consensus 51.0, while 1Y inflation expectations fell 0.4 pp to 4.2%. Rate hike expectations were volatile, ultimately settling at around 30bps of hikes though year-end, down 6bps from last week, though off the >40bps high at the start of the week after the ramp up in Middle East tensions.",
